<CohortPage
  title="The five-part prompt"
  kicker="handout · session 1"
  lead="Copy the template, fill in the blanks, and paste it into any AI tool. The more specific each part is, the less the tool has to guess."
>
  <Shared />

  <h2 id="your-task-in-one-sentence-session-1">Your task in one sentence (session 1)</h2>

  <blockquote>
    <p>Every week I do <strong>________</strong> using <strong>________</strong>, it takes <strong>________</strong>, and done means <strong>________</strong>.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <p><strong>By track</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Everyday AI:</strong> fill in the template as it is. If your task uses a file, describe its real shape in <em>Input</em>: the column names, the document type, how many rows.</li>
    <li><strong>Connect:</strong> pick a task that starts in your email or calendar. In <em>Input</em>, say which threads or meeting requests it starts from. In <em>Check</em>, say what you approve before anything is sent.</li>
    <li><strong>Build:</strong> under the template, list the steps an agent would take: where the input comes from, what the AI does, where it stops for your approval, and where the result goes. You'll use that list in session 3.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="homework">Homework</h2>

  <p>Run your prompt once on this week's real task, made safe first. Write down one place where it was wrong.</p>
</CohortPage>
